<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  BoxedVN ships exactly two entitlements, and each one is load-bearing.

	  get-task-allow
	      Lets a debugger attach to the app.  That is the mechanism StikDebug
	      and equivalent JIT enablers use, and attaching is what causes the
	      kernel to grant dynamic-codesigning, which is what makes
	      mmap(PROT_EXEC | MAP_JIT) succeed.  Without it Boxedwine's ARM64 JIT
	      cannot run at all.  Sideloading tools normally set this themselves;
	      it is declared here so an unsigned IPA carries the intent.

	  com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit
	      Boxedwine reserves a large contiguous region for the emulated guest
	      address space.  Without the raised limit the app is jetsammed on
	      devices with less RAM.  This entitlement is honoured only when the
	      signing identity is allowed to use it; free Apple IDs are not, and
	      signing tools strip it.  BoxedVN works without it on 6 GB+ devices,
	      so it is safe to remove.

	  Entitlements deliberately NOT present:
	      com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit and friends are macOS Hardened
	      Runtime keys and mean nothing on iOS.
	      com.apple.private.* keys require Apple-internal signing.
	      No hypervisor, USB or jailbreak entitlements: BoxedVN emulates in
	      userspace and needs none of them.

	  See docs/BUILD_IOS.md for what a signing tool may rewrite or drop.
	-->
	<key>get-task-allow</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
